@@ -1020,6 +1020,119 @@ Default: `visible`

 A shortcut for setting `overflowX` and `overflowY` at the same time.

+#### Grid
+
+Set `display="grid"` on a `Box` to lay out its children in a grid. By default, children fill the grid row by row, from left to right and top to bottom.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="2 2">
+	<Box>
+		<Text>A</Text>
+	</Box>
+	<Box>
+		<Text>B</Text>
+	</Box>
+	<Box>
+		<Text>C</Text>
+	</Box>
+	<Box>
+		<Text>D</Text>
+	</Box>
+</Box>
+// A B
+// C D
+```
+
+The existing [`gap`](#gap), [`columnGap`](#columngap), and [`rowGap`](#rowgap) properties also apply to grid tracks.
+
+##### gridTemplateColumns
+
+Type: `string`\
+Default: none
+
+Size of the grid's columns, as a space-separated list of track sizes. Supported track sizes:
+
+- A number of characters, for example `3`
+- `auto` — the track is sized to the largest item it contains
+- A fraction of the remaining space, for example `1fr`
+- `minmax(min, max)` — the track is at least `min` characters wide and grows up to `max`, where `max` is a number of characters or a fraction of the remaining space (for example `minmax(2, 1fr)`). When the maximum is a fraction of the remaining space, the space left over after satisfying every track's minimum is distributed proportionally among the fractional maximums
+
+If not set, the grid has a single auto-sized column, so children stack vertically.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="1fr 1fr" width={6}>
+	<Text>ab</Text>
+	<Text>cd</Text>
+	<Text>ef</Text>
+	<Text>gh</Text>
+</Box>
+// ab cd
+// ef gh
+```
+
+##### gridTemplateRows
+
+Type: `string`\
+Default: none
+
+Size of the grid's rows, as a space-separated list of track sizes (see `gridTemplateColumns`). If not set, rows are created automatically as needed.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="1" gridTemplateRows="1 1">
+	<Text>A</Text>
+	<Text>B</Text>
+	<Text>C</Text>
+	<Text>D</Text>
+</Box>
+// A
+// B
+// C
+// D
+```
+
+##### gridColumn
+
+Type: `number` | `string`\
+Default: auto
+
+Column where the child is placed: a single 1-based index, for example `2`, or a `"start / end"` string to span multiple columns, for example `"1 / 3"` (the item spans from column 1 to column 3).
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="2 2 2" gridTemplateRows="1 1">
+	<Box gridColumn={2}>
+		<Text>B</Text>
+	</Box>
+	<Box gridColumn={1} gridRow={2}>
+		<Text>D</Text>
+	</Box>
+	<Box gridColumn={3}>
+		<Text>C</Text>
+	</Box>
+	<Box gridColumn={2} gridRow={2}>
+		<Text>E</Text>
+	</Box>
+</Box>
+//   B C
+// D E
+```
+
+##### gridRow
+
+Type: `number` | `string`\
+Default: auto
+
+Row where the child is placed, in the same format as `gridColumn`.
+
+```jsx
+<Box display="grid" gridTemplateColumns="2 2" gridTemplateRows="1 1 1">
+	<Box gridRow="1 / 3">
+		<Text>A</Text>
+	</Box>
+	<Text>B</Text>
+</Box>
+// A B
+```
+
 #### Borders

